In the PCA on forms of capital run over the 39 hundred-year BCE time slices (BCE 4300-500; symbolic submatrix S = [Zhausgr, ZDolch, ZAxtSchwert]), the three symbolic-capital components are characterised in the following data-grounded way.

PC1 of the symbolic PCA absorbs 54.4% of the submatrix variance (PC2 adds 28.8%; together 83.2%). All three symbolic variables load with the SAME POSITIVE sign and with comparable magnitudes on PC1 - HouseSize +0.568, Dagger +0.662, HatchetSword +0.489 - with Dagger dominating (|0.662|), then HouseSize (|0.568|), then HatchetSword (|0.489|). The axis was sign-normalised using Dagger as the anchor (raw loading -0.6617, sign flipped by factor -1). Because the triad co-aligns on PC1, the 39 hundred-year slices separate cleanly into a low-capital pole - early-En slices BCE 4300-3900 all sit at PC1 = -1.37 - and a high-capital pole in which Late Neolithic BCE 1800 (PC1 = +3.35), Old Bronze Age BCE 1300 (+2.69) and BCE 1400 (+2.67) reach the joint maxima. PC1 scores across all slices span min=-1.37, q1=-0.80, median=-0.62, q3=+0.82, max=+3.35 (skew +0.99, right-tailed toward the Bronze-Age maximum). In short: on PC1, HouseSize, Dagger and HatchetSword define a SINGLE COHERENT SYMBOLIC-CAPITAL AXIS.

On PC2 the picture changes - once the common PC1 movement is removed, the three symbolic variables DIVIDE: HatchetSword loads at +0.791, HouseSize at -0.609 (opposite sign, both large in magnitude), and Dagger at -0.061 (essentially zero, ~|-0.06|). The axis was sign-normalised using HatchetSword as the anchor (raw loading -0.7908, factor -1). PC2 therefore scores the contrast between HatchetSword-rich and HouseSize-rich time slices while leaving Dagger indifferent on this axis. The distribution of the 39 per-slice PC2 scores is centred slightly below zero (min=-1.55, q1=-0.41, median=-0.13, q3=+0.51, max=+2.45; skew +0.81): long right tail driven by OBA BCE 1500-1600 reaching +2.45, single long lower tail from Early/Medium slices BCE 3500-3400 at -1.55; the bulk of the slices (interquartile range -0.41 to +0.51) cluster near zero, i.e. PC2 is a secondary, residual axis on which HouseSize, Dagger and HatchetSword are only weakly distinguished.

Supporting evidence from the full 12-capital PCA (PC1 = 31.8%, PC2 = 20.4% of total variance) shows the symbolic triad still all load positively on its PC1 (Zhausgr +0.228, ZDolch +0.279, ZAxtSchwert +0.301) even though PC1 of the full matrix is dominated by economic/material capital (ZCU_AU +0.399, Zkeverz +0.381, ZKeform +0.355). This independently confirms that the symbolic triad behaves as a coherent block on the leading axis of the full capital system.

DATA-GROUNDED HYPOTHESIS (one sentence): In the 100-year-sliced PCA of the capital matrix, the symbolic-capital components HouseSize, Dagger and HatchetSword are characterised as a SINGLE COHERENT BLOCK on PC1 (loadings all positive and similar - Zhausgr +0.568, ZDolch +0.662, ZAxtSchwert +0.489 - explaining 54.4% of the symbolic submatrix variance and tracking the En->LateN/OBA rise of symbolic wealth), while on PC2 they SEPARATE INTO A BIPOLAR CONTRAST (HatchetSword +0.791 vs HouseSize -0.609, with Dagger -0.061 essentially neutral), and the 39 per-slice PC2 scores are CENTRED NEAR ZERO AND MODERATELY SPREAD (min=-1.55, q1=-0.41, median=-0.13, q3=+0.51, max=+2.45, skew +0.81, dominated by OBA 1500-1600 BCE at +2.45).